From abe82e1793bea21abd467985e0383c8dbf643b61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:21:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add admin Field Activity log with Force Checkout and Reset
 GPS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Until now, nobody — not even an admin — had any way to close a stuck
open visit (sales_visits has RLS enabled with zero policies; every
read/write went through staff-only SECURITY DEFINER functions). A rep
whose phone dies right after check-in, or whose dealer has a wrong/stale
saved GPS location, was permanently stuck: checkout itself enforces a
100m geofence, so once they've left they can never satisfy it, and while
stuck they're also blocked from checking into any other dealer or ending
their day.

Adds a new admin-only "Field Activity" screen (/admin/visits):
- A full check-in/check-out activity log across every rep and dealer
  (admin_get_all_visits RPC), searchable and filterable by status.
- "Force Checkout" — an emergency override (admin_force_checkout RPC)
  that closes a stuck open visit without the geofence or photo/video
  requirements, gated on a required reason and flagged forced_checkout
  (with who/why) so it never looks like a normal field checkout.
- "Reset GPS" — clears a dealer's saved location_lat/lng (via the
  existing admin-write RLS policy on profiles, no new RPC needed) so
  the next check-in there sets a correct location fresh, fixing dealers
  whose stored GPS was captured wrong or has gone stale.

Both server functions re-check public.is_admin() themselves — the
screen being admin-gated client-side is not the real authorization.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxWPdEf21EL6SvRpGBbX8q
